WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:15.727
Domain and limits
Study where x cubed minus three x increases and decreases. The function is
defined on all real numbers, with limits negative and positive infinity at the
two ends.

2
00:00:15.727 --> 00:00:27.818
Factor the derivative
The derivative is three x squared minus three. Factor it as three times x
minus one times x plus one.

3
00:00:27.818 --> 00:00:40.818
Study the sign
The derivative vanishes at minus one and one. The product is positive before
minus one, negative between them, and positive after one.

4
00:00:40.818 --> 00:00:54.727
Calculate significant values
The function therefore increases, then decreases, then increases again.
Calculate the significant values to obtain two at minus one and minus two at
one.

5
00:00:54.727 --> 00:01:11.364
Build the variation table
There is a local maximum of two and a local minimum of minus two. The
variation table combines these values with the limits so the sketch follows
from the calculations.
